<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Chapter 66 — Latency, Tail Latency, Virtual Threads vs Reactive.
    quote/     QuoteServer: one endpoint (three sequential downstream calls) in four concurrency models: blocking on
               200 platform threads, blocking on virtual threads, the same with a limit of 300 in flight, and
               non-blocking on two event-loop threads
    backend/   Backend: a downstream service with a fast path and a slow tail
    tail/      FanOut: calls to n backends at once, optionally hedged, with a hedging budget
    pinning/   Pinning: virtual threads blocking inside synchronized, for JDK 21 and JDK 24+
  verify/run.sh measures the four models under open load, fan-out tails with and without hedging, and pinning.
-->
